v0.96.18
	Switching to build via CMake and PicoSDK

[02/28/2025]
v0.96.17
	For mobile murmulator:
		additional LCD settings in the settings file

[01/28/2025]
v0.96.16
	The video output auto-detection algorithm has been changed.
	
[01/21/2025]
v0.96.15
	Edited [POKE] to the working state, and from the files.pok can also be used, 
	The algorithm is as follows: you load the game and then either enter it in decimal from the [POKE] menu with your hands,
	or select the desired items from the file and then you can play.
	
	Separate mapping of 2 joysticks and keyboard to all old mapping options.
	Automatic detection of VGA/HDMI/TFT screen.
	Pin and frequency selection for HardTS.
	For mobile murmulator:
		Automatic detection of battery monitoring - ADC/MAX17043
		Volume control via SELECT+UP/DOWN
		Screen brightness control via SELECT+LEFT/RIGHT
		Lock input via SELECT+A, unlock via SELECT+B

[21.06.2024]
v0.96.14 
	Various bugfixes.
	Support for I2S PCM DACs.
	
[12.04.2024]
v0.96.04
	Redesigned the TFT driver into a common unified VGA/HDMI/TFT display driver.
	I remind you of the pinout for connecting SPI TFT screens ST7789, ST7789V, ILI9341, ILI9341V, GC9A01
		TFT_CS_PIN (6)
		TFT_RST_PIN (8)
		TFT_LED_PIN (9)
		TFT_DC_PIN (10)
		TFT_DATA_PIN (12)
		TFT_CLK_PIN (13)
	The following items have been added to the settings:
		[LCD Rotate] - Rotate the image of the LCD screen
		[LCD inversion] - Inversion of the LCD screen image
		[LCD Pixel format] - The pixel format of the LCD screen
	Correction of the on-screen keyboard.
	Reading the headlines .tap and .trd is placed in a separate buffer and does not affect the download
	
	Switching joysticks via START+UP and START+DOWN
	Quick save/load via joystick combinations:
		START+LEFT - save
		START+RIGHT - load
	Quick on-screen keyboard call: START+A
	Quick call to the file manager: START+B
	Added a composite output driver using an external encoder on the CXA1645M chip.
	A software composite output driver has been added.
	Improved keyboard handling.
	Added a button to close the current image.tap - F9.	
	
[05.02.2024]
v0.95
	The HDMI driver from Alex Ekb (@Alex_Eburg) has been added. Now the assembly is performed in 4 versions: VGA, HDMI, TFT_ILI9341, TFT_ST7789v
	Changing the mapping of buttons:
		[F11] - Turning on/off the HUD
		[F12]/[PrnScreen] - Quick menu call (joystick menu)
	Control change:
		The joystick is additionally plugged into Cursor Joy at the same time as Kempston Joy, while as an experiment, we will disable it.
		For the Wii joystick, auto-firing on X and Y has been added, when working in mouse mode, the left stick works as a scroll wheel.
	File Manager:
		Added file deletion.
			To delete, mark the required files or folders by placing the cursor on the required file and pressing the "Space" or "Insert" key, the file names will change their color to yellow.
			To start the file deletion procedure, press the key combination "Shift+Delete", after which a dialog box will appear confirming this action.

	[New category: Plans]
		1. Processing .pok files and manual input of Poke (immortality in games).
		2. Universal button mapping (joystick->buttons,buttons->buttons).
		3. Joystick mode indication.
		4. Support Ch9350 (USB->UART) converter on PS/2 keyboard port.
		5. Support.tzx files, and suddenly it will work ;)
		6. Support for .scl files, and suddenly it will work ;)
		7. PS/2 mouse on the joystick port.
		8. A real i2c disk drive on the joystick port.
		9. Memory expansion due to SPI PSRAM.
	This list is compiled from memory and the sequence of development may differ from the above.

